<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore March bank credit rises 14.4 pct on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore March bank credit rises 14.4 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank credit to non-bank customers (in billions of Singapore dollars):</p>
<p>						   Mar 97  Feb 97  Mar 96</p>
<p>Total (including financial bills)	129.45  128.74  113.16</p>
<p>Agriculture, mining, quarrying (millions)  218.0   181.3   147.7</p>
<p>Manufacturing				   12.4    12.27   11.71</p>
<p>Building, construction			42.92   42.52   35.95</p>
<p>General commerce				23.75   24.15   21.73</p>
<p>Transport, storage, communication	  2.95    2.86    2.33</p>
<p>Financial institutions			19.49   19.50   17.20</p>
<p>Personal loans				  21.05   20.61   18.11</p>
<p>Others					     6.68    6.64    5.98</p>
<p>The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said in its monthly report bank credit grew marginally slower in March at 14.4 percent compared with 15 percent year-on-year in February.</p>
<p>Growth of credit extended to the manufacturing sector fell to 5.9 percent compared with 8.8 percent in February.</p>
<p>Bank loans to non-bank customers and the commerce sector decreased to 13.3 percent and 9.3 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Loans to the transport sector picked up in March, accelerating to 22.4 percent from 26.7 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Credit extended to professional and private individuals also grew faster by 16.2 percent compared with 15.5 percent the month previously.</p>
<p>Growth of lending to the building and construction sector fell slightly to 19.4 percent while that to other sectors expanded by 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
